course: dictionary
lesson: 3317
title: European: a place, a person, or a describing word
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: European is a word you will see often in geography and history. It can describe things, or it can name a person. When it comes before a noun, it is an adjective: «European countries» are countries from or in Europe, the continent that includes France, Germany, Spain, Ireland and the UK.
explain: When European stands alone, it is a noun: a person from Europe. In «Long before Europeans came», the -s shows there is more than one person. Look at the words around it to decide which kind of word you have.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it in. In «a European city», try "a city from Europe". If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right. Europe is a continent, so a European city is a city on that continent.
fact: European is an adjective when it describes a noun, as in «European countries» or «a European city».
fact: European is a noun when it names a person from Europe: «Long before Europeans came».
fact: Europe is a continent. It includes countries such as France, Germany, Spain, Ireland and the UK.
fact: The European Union is a group of European countries. Its name uses European as an adjective.
fact: Geography lessons often ask you to learn European countries, capitals and rivers.
exercise: In «European countries», which word tells you what kind of countries they are? | *European | they | kind | countries
exercise: What is a European, as a noun? | A capital city | A river in Germany | A country in Africa | *A person from Europe
exercise: What does European describe in «beaver fur for European hats»? | symbol | *hats | fur | beaver
test: In «After 1492 diseases carried by Europeans killed very many native people», who carried the diseases? | The Aztecs | *Europeans | Native people | The Inca
test: Which of these is a European city? | Sydney | *Paris | Cairo | Mumbai
exam: In «Long before Europeans came, the Indian Ocean was a busy trade world», who does Europeans mean? | Native Americans | *People from Europe | Traders from China | Sailors from Africa
